	(text "S3: SHORT-CIRCUIT BOOSTER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.222 153.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "099dbdc3-2060-54d0-b4ac-f437d312e588")
	)
	(text "S3: DRIVER AND 2 GATES"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 321.965 19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "198ddca5-30c0-5f53-80b8-4454894d44e2")
	)
	(text "DESAT > 10.3-10.9 V (above the 10.0 V maximum trip of the -Q1 grade) -> MMBT3904 -> MMBT3906 charges BG to VEE + 10 V;\nper device AO3400A + 22R pull the gate to VEE; BG holds ~3 us (1k + FET gates)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.222 216.792 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4c3189b1-670d-5607-ab17-42cdb389112e")
	)
	(text "UCC14241-Q1, 24 V in, regulated +/-1.3 %, reinforced barrier.\nRDR: RLIM1 sources COM, RLIM2 + DLIM sink it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 183.189 131.948 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6038206b-7e5d-54d6-ba2a-a3e2d62ccea1")
	)
	(text "DESAT pin (internal 500 uA blanking source, trip 8.5-10.0 V) - Rs - 2 x BYG23T-M3/TR (1300 V each) - drain.\nBAT54S keeps DX between COM and VDD against dv/dt through the string; Cblk footprint DNP."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.522 211.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6056baf4-5401-5ca9-bfd4-61f3438375fe")
	)
	(text "MMBT3906 inverter (E COM, base BAT54+2.2k on CLAMP) drives CG to COM once the lowest gate is below ~-1.2 V;\nMMBT3904 release (from OUTH via 5.6 V Zener) holds CG at VEE while OUTH drives."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 241.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9af9e508-08ad-5ec0-b9dc-1e33947b306e")
	)
	(text "S3: DESAT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 246.522 153.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a7666496-50f9-5100-96ea-354189a74788")
	)
	(text "Per device: Ron/Roff, 0.5R Kelvin R to the COM star, 10k and Zeners (about +21 V / -5.7 V) on its own Kelvin net.\nMiller hold: N-MOSFET clamp (PMV30ENEA) gate-pin to a local VEE (1u on the Kelvin pin). LAYOUT: FET + 1u at the device, loop <= 1 nH."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 321.965 140.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a7d162b6-9d5c-5670-b39a-39e798c6189e")
	)
	(text "IN+ = own PWM; IN- = complementary switch, falling edge stretched 4.02k/100p\n(interlock + min dead time = max(firmware, hardware)). Bias PG (active low) pulls RDY low."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 89.052 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c141fc0b-49ff-552b-90b3-04e676255652")
	)
	(text "SYMMETRY: gate and Kelvin of S3a/S3b as coupled pairs of equal length (+/-10 %) from the COM_S3 star; Ron,\nRoff, Kelvin R, 10k, Zeners at each device; power sources joined only by the busbar. CLAMP LOOP: each\nAO3400A + C_VL at its device's gate-Kelvin pins, loop <= 1 nH. IC-22: milled slot between the drain\npin 1 and pins 2-4 of each TO-247-4L; DESAT string >= 2.5 mm pad gap per diode; board coated to PD1.\nMiller hold (gdrv rev 5, ngspice 1100 V / 72.4 A, 115 V/ns): die +1.41 V vs VGS(th) min 1.94 V at 175 C,\nmargin 0.53 V (rev 4 PNP: +2.14 V) - BENCH TEST (double pulse, hot, minimum-threshold devices)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 356.744 179.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c4a0a534-7d6e-5689-bd7d-b1f173458439")
	)
	(text "S3: MILLER CLAMP CONTROL"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 153.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
